  "name": "Young Person’s CORE (YP-CORE)",
  "short_name": null,
  "language": "en",
  "description": "The Young Person’s Clinical Outcomes in Routine Evaluation (YP-CORE) is a 10 item self-report measure designed for monitoring treatment outcomes in young people aged between 11 and 16 years of age. It was derived from the adult measure Clinical Outcomes in Routine Evaluation – Outcome Measure (CORE-OM), and captures a range of presenting problems relevant for mental health services. The copyright holder for the YP-CORE is the CORE System Trust.",
